  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Bilateral (multi country) Security Assistance Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment provides a multi-country mechanism to enhance security sector engagement in partner countries through bilateral cooperation. BSAP is a mechanism by which Australia provides targeted bilateral support to partner countries not delivered through existing mechanisms to help them meet their unique security challenges. BSAP will focus on delivering on commitments made by Australia in bilateral security instruments and working with PICs to establish bilateral security instruments where they have yet to be developed. BSAP contributes to the Boe Declaration goal of a secure and resilient region of sovereign states through good governance, individual liberty under the law, upholding democratic processes and institutions and recognising the vulnerability of member countries to threats to their security. BSAP supports activities under three pillars: 1) Border security, 2) Transnational crime, and 3) Governance and Resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
